[h2]Fixed: Atlantis is now genuinely unreachable, the sea voyage included[/h2]

[b]The previous update took Atlantis off the portal page, but a player who owns the Atlantis DLC could still sail there.[/b] Atlantis is disabled in this mod, so a clean act list was only half the job. This update closes the travel route itself.

[list]
[*][b]The Rhodes to Gadir voyage is closed.[/b] Atlantis does not branch off the end of the campaign, it branches off Rhodes, in the middle of Immortal Throne, on the mandatory route to Hades. That is why the two earlier act caps never touched it: both of those close post Hades transitions. The quest NPC who starts the Atlantis adventure and the ship captain who carries you west are both suppressed, so the route no longer opens.
[*][b]The Gadir to Atlantis landing is closed too[/b], at its own link rather than only upstream, so there is no single point of failure.
[*][b]The two Tartarus act portals are closed[/b] by the same method already proven on the Act 5 cap, as defence in depth.
[*][b]Immortal Throne era travel is untouched.[/b] Only the two Atlantis DLC boat NPCs are hidden. Rhodes itself is unchanged: you can still walk it, fight in it, use its portal and its shops. If you own the DLC, Rhodes now looks the way it already looks for a player who does not.
[*][b]The return boats were deliberately left working.[/b] If you sailed west on an earlier build and have a character standing in Gadir, Malta or Atlantis, you can still sail back. Stranding a character would have been the one change worse than the leak.
[*][b]The portal page is unchanged and re-checked[/b]: four act tabs, Greece, Egypt, Orient and Immortal Throne, with Olympus and all of Hades still listed.
[*][b]A permanent gate so it cannot come back.[/b] The build now derives the list of routes that could still reach Atlantis and fails loudly unless that list is empty. It also fails if the cap reaches too far and touches an Atlantis record it was never meant to. It is checked against four deliberately broken builds.
[/list]

[i]This update changes six database records only. No stat, skill, monster, quest, map or text was touched. The craft chain, the armour and loot distribution balance, the uber orb weapon breadth, the portal page cap, the Epic and Legendary soul names and the chest breadth work from the previous updates are all included.[/i]
